  "published": "2026-10-31T18:30:55.2Z",
  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "0.8.9: decoding and ToJpeg charge their working memory against MaxPixels (64 bytes per allowed pixel plus 64 MiB), so a small file declaring many extra channels can no longer allocate gigabytes, and MaxFrames counts frames that are not displayed. Cancellation now stops a 12 MP encode within 35 ms (it could take over 100 ms). Fuzzing of cancellation at every allocation, failing streams, returned buffers, the encoder and metadata editing found no other defect. Decoded pixels and encoded bytes are unchanged. No API changes. See docs/releases/release-0.8.9.md and docs/design/0.8.9-resilience.md.",
